-- UNKNOWN MEMBER TYPE -------------------------------------------- src/Main.fic

This use of `sum` needs a type that has the members `add` and `zero`, but I
cannot tell which type that is:

14|     Debug.log "r" (sum [ 1, 2, 3 ]) |> always ()
                       ^^^
    add : number -> number -> number
    zero : number

The type is not determined here. If this definition is meant to work for every
type that has these members, it needs a type annotation with a `where` block (a
constraint is never inferred):

    where
        a has add : ...
        a has zero : ...

Otherwise a type annotation on the value that is used here will settle it.

The type is a `number` variable, which only the built-in types can be. The
built-in types (`Int`, `Float`, `String`, `List`, records, tuples, ...) do not
have members yet; they get them in a later version. For now a constraint can
only be met by a custom type that defines the member in its `where` block.
